repository-code: "https://github.com/madainsaleh2/fks-sanger-pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Automated detection of FKS1 and FKS2 hotspot mutations from paired Sanger
  sequencing chromatograms in Nakaseomyces glabratus. Performs quality
  trimming, forward/reverse consensus assembly, translation, and variant
  calling with explicit quality gates. Reports mutations only; no clinical
  interpretation is applied.
keywords:
  - Sanger sequencing
  - Nakaseomyces glabratus
  - Candida glabrata
  - FKS1
  - FKS2
  - bioinformatics
